Some of you will be familiar with the Dining Philosophers problem.
Basically, you have 5 philosophers sitting around a circular table with 5
forks on it. A philosopher needs 2 forks to eat. They get the forks by
reaching for a fork, and if it's not available they wait until it is. It's
possible to get a situation where they can never get it - imagine they all
pick up the fork on their right, then wait forever for the one on their
left - and so they starve to death. The solution is to add a security
guard in so that only 4 philosophers at a time can sit down at the table. 

But what does this have to do with Nethack, you ask? I recently had to
code up an animation of this problem in a language called Occam. As an
attempt to do something slightly different, I did it in a nethack stylee,
and thought you fine people might fancy a peek. You can download linux and
solaris binaries at http://www.hornyvegan.com/code.php. As I say, I don't
really want to make the source publically available, as it's an
assessment, but if you really fancy a peek drop me an email. There's a
screenshot at the above URL so if you're using a slightly obsolete OS [:)]
you can have a gander. 

